  "agent": {
    "note": "**TAKE 4 — white default** (founder on take 3, with Make screenshots: \"transparent bg is poor when the background is also black. we need to default to white\").\n\n- `background` defaults to **white** (`DEFAULT_BACKGROUND` + `defaultProps`); the Background segmented control now opens on White. Transparent stays one click away for trace/overlay work — the Layout page's Transparent / trace styles already pass it explicitly, so they are unchanged.\n- Side effect worth knowing: the perf-heatmap PNGs (electron, no background prop) now sit on white instead of transparent.\n- Grid default, explicit debug defaults, preset-decides-mode, grid-paper lattice, and the four engine/CLI fixes all stand. No cover.\n\nStress twins re-frozen AND stills re-rendered (01/02/03/05/06 now sit on white; 04 already asked for white).",
    "question": "White default reads right? Then stress-01..10. Still open: core-vs-publisher (rec. CORE) · internal:true? (rec. no) · grid-paper keep/prune · label → \"Wireframe\"?"
  },
